          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8058adb57d133b575329932deb75abebe9668906",
          "message": "fix: Allow to pass any object with .toJSON method to JSON field (#20259)\n\n* fix: Allow to pass any object with .toJSON method to JSON field\r\n\r\nThat used to work in GraphQL protocol and JS. Technically, it's an\r\n\"accidental\" feature and it does not work on TS level. After some\r\ninternal discussions, we've decided to make it a proper feature (and\r\nalso fix TS part of it).\r\n\r\nOne more thing this PR does: for non-serializable values, it will show\r\nrich error message with context, rather internal one, thrown by\r\n`assertNever`. Since query arguments come from untrusted user input,\r\nrelying on a fixed type for them was incorrect to begin with.\r\nFix #20192\r\n\r\n* Restore commended out code\r\n\r\n* Update packages/client/src/runtime/core/jsonProtocol/serializeJsonQuery.ts\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Joël Galeran <Jolg42@users.noreply.github.com>\r\n\r\n* Update packages/client/tests/functional/query-validation/tests.ts\r\n\r\n* Update packages/client/src/runtime/core/jsonProtocol/serializeJsonQuery.ts\r\n\r\n* Update message/snapshots\r\n\r\n* Fix type test\r\n\r\n---------\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Joël Galeran <Jolg42@users.noreply.github.com>",
