          "message": "feat(cli): Support `prisma platform auth show --sensitive` (#24745)\n\n## Changes\r\nWhen the user adds a `--sensitive` option when running `prisma platform auth token show`, we include the current auth token in the output\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nnpx prisma platform auth show --sensitive\r\n```\r\n\r\n ## Context\r\nThis would allows users to provide the token explicitly for us to authenticate for Optimize in cases like docker or codespaces, where we aren't able to hit the temporary local server the cli creates for auth purposes.\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nnew PrismaClient().$extends(withOptimize({\r\n  // in this case the user stored the token the cli logged in (1), then provided it as an env var\r\n  token: process.env.PLATFORM_TOKEN\r\n}))\r\n```\r\n\r\n ## Links\r\n* Discussion: https://prisma-company.slack.com/archives/C04FDERNP32/p1720522326387089\r\n* Ticket: https://linear.app/prisma-company/issue/EXP-135/prisma-optimize-login-in-docker\r\n* Related issue: https://github.com/prisma/optimize-feedback/issues/3\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: pierre <pierreantoine.urvoy@gmail.com>",
          "timestamp": "2024-07-12T13:04:29+02:00",
          "tree_id": "67fe724c16401f5ef36f4985e93bc1a00fb1170e",
