          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c1e58fd4fe039bffa2e3da04115a5425d60eaf99",
          "message": "feat: change default output location in `prisma init` (#26577)\n\nDon't suggest generating in `node_modules` by default in `prisma init`\nand instead generate in the source tree.\n\nThe base directory for the location of the generated client is chosen\nbased on the following rules:\n- If there's a `tsconfig.json` and it explicitly defines the root\ndirectory, we use that\n- If there's a directory called `src`, `lib` or `app`, we use that (in\nthis order)\n- Otherwise we use the current directory\n\nIn this directory, we create `generated/prisma`.\n\nThe directory is chosen in anticipation of getting rid of the `index.js`\nbarrel file in the future ESM client and introducing the `client.ts`\nentrypoint, so that the full import path would be\n`./generated/prisma/client`. If we used `generated/prisma/client` as the\noutput now, we'd have to change it again, otherwise we'd end up with\n`./generated/prisma/client/client`. To ease the transition, we'll add\nthe alternative `client` entrypoint in the current client as well.\n\nCloses:\nhttps://linear.app/prisma-company/issue/ORM-777/update-prisma-init-to-include-a-custom-outputpath-in-the-default",
