          "distinct": true,
          "id": "0fa294aa0c67759375aeb92de78c6dc6b3135338",
          "message": "refactor(schema path): ORM-667 remove schema path dependency from further classes (#26596)\n\nThis PR further replaces the usage of `schemaPath` with the new\n`schemaContext` introduced in\nhttps://github.com/prisma/prisma/pull/26588.\n\nThese changes aim to achieve three primary goals:\n- A) Refactor towards a dependency injected model for our schema data.\n- B) Centralize further everything that gets derived from the schema\npath.\n- C) Remove redundant IO schema loading calls.\n\nMain changes:\n- Use `schemaContext` in `prisma generate` and generators.\n- Use `schemaContext` in introspection code paths.\n- Use `schemaContext` in `Migrate` and `SchemaEngine` class.\n- Remove unused code paths & options that used `schemaPath` in `getDMMF`\n& `getConfig`.\n\nNext up in a follow up PR:\n- Migrate views, migration and sql directory paths into the\n`schemaContext`. (https://github.com/prisma/prisma/pull/26631)\n- Untangle the `checkUnsupportedDataProxy` method.\n- Try to remove further schemaPath dependencies in the generator\nimplementation.\n- Remove legacy verifySeedConfig code.\n(https://github.com/prisma/prisma/pull/26624)\n\n\nref [ORM-667: Untangle uses of schema-path in the\ncodebase](https://linear.app/prisma-company/issue/ORM-667/untangle-uses-of-schema-path-in-the-codebase)",
