          "distinct": true,
          "id": "403f21f545cf1cd7b81e19ea4c3fc41b211b6667",
          "message": "fix(cli): don't use `readConfigFile` from `typescript` package (#26698)\n\n`typescript` is a peer dependency of `prisma` and thus is not bundled by\nesbuild, which makes the CLI crash when trying to unconditionally import\n`readConfigFile` if `typescript` is not installed since\n<https://github.com/prisma/prisma/pull/26577>.\n\nThis commit replaces the import of `readConfigFile` (which, despite the\nname, is just a generic JSONC file reader) with a third-party package\n`get-tsconfig` that provides the proper tsconfig reading functionality\nand typed results, which also allows us to remove the validation logic\n(together with the Effect Schema dependency) and `extends` property\nresolution from our code. `get-tsconfig` is self-contained and has no\ndependency on `typescript` or other packages.\n\nWe already depend on `get-tsconfig` as a dev dependency, transitively\nvia `tsx` and `eslint-plugin-import-x`.\n\nThanks to @viktor-ferenczi for the suggestion!",
          "timestamp": "2025-03-21T09:02:00Z",
          "tree_id": "44820df148f18ab2937c728c56043ae164185f4d",
          "url": "https://github.com/prisma/prisma/commit/403f21f545cf1cd7b81e19ea4c3fc41b211b6667"
