          "id": "e3f2a18f4b458caa9f2be1282a7c929211ea2c8c",
          "message": "test: add initial type benchmarks (#26894)\n\nThis PR uses\n[`@ark/attest`](https://github.com/arktypeio/arktype/tree/main/ark/attest#benches)\nto add type-level benchmarks for several schemas + usage patterns in\n`packages/cli/src/__tests__/benches`.\n\nThe benchmarks can be run simply by executing the associated TS file (or\nthrough the `package.json` scripts in each bench dir that do the same).\n\nInitial results were extremely good- linear scaling across all tested\nAPIs.\n\nThough client extensions add some general overhead, it along with the\nother APIs tested here should be able to scale quite far before type\nperformance becomes an issue.\n\nMost importantly, these benchmarks server as a pattern to adapt to other\nAPIs + patterns that could cause problematic type performance in the\nfuture.\n\nIf anyone is aware of a relatively minimal repro (think ~10 models and\n<=50 ops) for bad type performance, I'd love to take a look. Otherwise,\nit should be easy enough to add them here in the future and start\ntesting!\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Florian Goessler <florian.goessler@hey.com>\nCo-authored-by: Prismo <52275815+prisma-bot@users.noreply.github.com>",
