          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3db9675fa7fc0d5f70e3721f9c66c0e08d966e4f",
          "message": "fix: ORM-924 fix leaking env vars (#27106)\n\nDue to recent refactoring changes in our env var and schema loading we\nintroduced a bug (see https://github.com/prisma/prisma/issues/27074)\nwhere during the code generation step at the end of `prisma migrate dev`\nvalues from `env(...)` statements in the schema file could end up in the\ngenerated code output.\n\nNote that this was NOT the case during a regular `prisma generate`. =>\nAs users are NOT expected to run `prisma migrate dev` with production\ncredentials and are not expected to commit the generated code this is\nunlikely to have leaked actual production credentials into generated\ncode or source control systems.\n\nThis bug was likely introduced in version 6.6.0.\n\nThis PR includes an E2E tests that checks our generated output against\nany content from the provided env var.\n\nFixes #27074 \nFixes ORM-924",
          "timestamp": "2025-05-07T10:36:07+02:00",
          "tree_id": "539b91705ce30674a17cd5ee70ecd6b0b41ad4b6",
