          "distinct": true,
          "id": "15ecb4ee124035a112e39691fd18068e7d1b8817",
          "message": "fix(client): revamp ClientEngine initialization and shutdown (#27528)\n\nRefactor the initialization and shutdown logic in the `ClientEngine`:\n\n* Get rid of messy interdependent `Promise`s stored as class fields and\nintroduce an explicit state machine with a discrete number of states and\nclearly defined transitions between them. All methods are safely\ncallable concurrently and in any sequence because they know how to\nhandle each of the four possible states. `ClientEngine` now starts\ndisconnected and connects lazily on the first query, just like\n`LibraryEngine`.\n\t```mermaid\n\tstateDiagram-v2\n\t    [*] --> disconnected\n\t\n\t    disconnected --> connecting: #ensureStarted called\n\t    connecting --> connected: Connection promise resolved\n\t    connecting --> disconnected: Connection promise rejected\n\t    connected --> disconnecting: stop called\n\t    disconnecting --> disconnected: Disconnect promise settled\n\t```\n* Make sure we discard the query compiler on panic and never use the\nsame instance again to avoid memory leaks.\n* Immediately drop the query compiler instance on WASM side on\ndisconnect instead of relying on `FinalizationRegistry` to maybe free it\nsome time later. Previously we would have a guaranteed memory leak on\nCloudflare Workers here but they [shipped `FinalizationRegistry` support\na couple of weeks\nago](https://blog.cloudflare.com/we-shipped-finalizationregistry-in-workers-why-you-should-never-use-it/).\nHowever, just like the linked article says, the cleanup callbacks are\nnot guaranteed to run, and we should call `free` directly if possible\nand only rely on GC hooks as a safety net.\n* Fix `getErrorMessageWithLink` being passed a random query that\nhappened to be started last instead of the query that actually failed,\nwhen multiple queries are in flight.\n\nRefs: https://github.com/prisma/prisma/pull/27493\nFixes: https://github.com/prisma/prisma/issues/27157\nCloses:\nhttps://linear.app/prisma-company/issue/ORM-972/bug-regression-driver-adapter-disconnect-issues",
          "timestamp": "2025-06-27T12:55:45+02:00",
          "tree_id": "f97ceaf463749a5be7ff37ce06a071056c5739a6",
          "url": "https://github.com/prisma/prisma/commit/15ecb4ee124035a112e39691fd18068e7d1b8817"
