          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c7370911a091a0a61a7a394391996e7231a9c2ce",
          "message": "feat(config): support `c12` (#27672)\n\nThis PR:\n- closes\n[ORM-1216](https://linear.app/prisma-company/issue/ORM-1216/prismaconfigts-support-multiple-extensions-ts-js-mjs-cjs-mts-cts-and)\n- replaces [`jiti`](https://github.com/unjs/jiti) with\n[`c12`](https://github.com/unjs/c12), which incorporates\n[`jiti`](https://github.com/unjs/jiti) itself, but uses the standard\nconfiguration loading approach already adopted by the the `unjs` / Nuxt\necosystem.\n- introduces support for `prisma.config.(js|ts|mjs|cjs|mts|cts)`\n- introduces support `.config/prisma.(js|ts|mjs|cjs|mts|cts)`\n- configuration files are evaluated on based on the file extension,\nfollowing the order `['.js', '.ts', '.mjs', '.cjs', '.mts', '.cts']`\n- introduces lots of tests, mostly drawing the example cases from\nexisting `prisma.config.ts` tests\n\nNote: we may need to modify tests in\n[packages/internals/src/__tests__/directoryConfig.test.ts](https://github.com/prisma/prisma/blob/4b4215f01b432b812438e9fd7988f7c1658e0718/packages/internals/src/__tests__/directoryConfig.test.ts)\nas well.\n\n---\n\nCurrently, `c12` tries to load `.json(c)` files too if it cannot find\nany JavaScript/TypeScript Prisma Config files.\nThis is documented via tests. It shouldn't be that big of a deal, but we\ncan address this in a follow-up PR, by either forking `c12`\n(recommended, until our changes make it upstream) or patching it\nlocally.\n\n---\n\nNote: we can merge this first and later patch/fork `c12`. Please refer\nthe comments in the tests.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jkomyno <12381818+jkomyno@users.noreply.github.com>",
