          "id": "99de31b95d8eda03658b9db9beeb8f7437cf280f",
          "message": "chore: ORM-1293 improve type benchmarks (#27775)\n\nThis PR (fixes and) extends our type performance tests. \n\nIt especially provides more examples and detailed insights into how\nproviding client options and client extensions make the type performance\nchecks slow.\n\nNoteable insights:\n- It's not just the log config that causes slow type checks.\n- Basically any non-empty client config - even just `adapter` or\n`datasourceUrl` - cause an explosion of type instantiations.\n- Applying a client extension BEFORE passing the client further around\ncan have the same POSITIVE performance impact as the `typeof`\nworkaround.\n- Using the `typeof` workaround, type instantiations don't even scale up\nwith schema size. Without it they dramatically scale up with schema\nsize.\n- Client extensions without custom client options do not cause a type\ninstantiations explosion and scale okay with schema size.",
