          "id": "9d18d2879e34fa3574e2b1d1c4a8e5dcd8861187",
          "message": "feat(client-generator-ts): use base64 encoding on Wasm files loaded by Node.js (#27795)\n\nThis PR:\n- closes\n[ORM-1316](https://linear.app/prisma-company/issue/ORM-1316/prisma-client-encode-wasm-binaries-as-base64-modules-on-non-edge-non)\n- closes https://github.com/prisma/prisma/issues/27754\n- closes https://github.com/prisma/prisma/issues/27083\n- closes https://github.com/prisma/prisma/issues/27572\n- closes https://github.com/prisma/prisma-examples/issues/8250\n- closes https://github.com/prisma/prisma-examples/issues/8249\n- when using `prisma-client` generator with `runtime = \"nodejs\"` (which\nis the default case), we stop attempting to read `.wasm` binaries via\n`fs`, and we rather import their base64-encoded definition from a\n`.wasm-base64.js` file resolved from `@prisma/client/runtime`.\n- I had previously tried to resolve these new `.wasm-base64.js` file\nfrom the local generated folder (within `./internals`), which worked\nwith e.g. `next dev` and `nuxt preview`, but it failed with `nuxt dev`.\n- this PR should solve most Wasm-loading issues related to\n`prisma-client` and `queryCompiler`.\n\n---\n\nLatest integration version:\nprisma@6.14.0-integration-feat-client-wasm-base64-on-nodejs.6\n\n/integration\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jkomyno <12381818+jkomyno@users.noreply.github.com>",
