          "distinct": true,
          "id": "77763f4aa2ec358e7174ff7c4ebf7fb4dda8a05a",
          "message": "refactor: replace `read-package-up` with `empathic` (#27814)\n\nIt looks like `@prisma/config` exploded in size after #27672, going from\n[2.9MB](https://pkg-size.dev/@prisma/config@6.12) to\n[34MB](https://pkg-size.dev/@prisma/config@6.13)(!!!) in install size\nand going from [one](https://npmgraph.js.org/?q=%40prisma%2Fconfig@6.13)\nsubdependency to\n[46](https://npmgraph.js.org/?q=%40prisma%2Fconfig@6.13). This pull\nrequest attempts to improve the situation by replacing `read-package-up`\nwith [`empathic`](https://github.com/lukeed/empathic), a fast and modern\nalternative made by someone from the Svelte team.\n\n`empathic` has [zero](https://npmgraph.js.org/?q=empathic)\nsubdependencies and is [21KB](https://pkg-size.dev/empathic) in install\nsize, while `read-package-up` has [20\nsubdependencies](https://npmgraph.js.org/?q=read-package-up) and is\n[1.6MB](https://pkg-size.dev/read-package-up) in size. This PR won't fix\nthe package size problem but at least it aims to improve it somewhat.\nSee the [before](https://npmgraph.js.org/?q=%40prisma%2Fconfig@6.13) and\n[after](https://npmgraph.js.org/?q=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FSuperchupuDev%2Fprisma%2Fblob%2Fc6a26927f98cc0e431df8ba5bc0accb3250b1a72%2Fpackages%2Fconfig%2Fpackage.json)\ncomparison.\n\nThe reason `read-package-up` is so huge is because it contains a lot of\nfunctionality simply not used here, mainly package normalization and a\ncustom JSON parser. Also, it's ESM only so it has to be dynamically\nimported each time `loadConfigFromPackageJson` is called, unlike\n`empathic` which provides dual exports.\n\n---\n\nThis PR closes https://github.com/prisma/prisma/issues/27774.",
