          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d4ec055ee9e13e62351bf72643fc978b3d315ae3",
          "message": "chore(ci): create tags on release (#28440)\n\nPreviously we relied on the git tags being created manually (via GitHub\nUI) when creating a new release. This led to occasional human errors\nwhere wrong commits were tagged when new commits were pushed right after\nthe release, as well as to a delay in creating the tags compared to\npublishing the release on npm.\n\nAs previously [agreed][], we're changing the process to have the tags\npushed automatically from CI, and then a GitHub release with release\nnotes being created manually afterwards.\n\n[agreed]:\nhttps://prisma-company.slack.com/archives/C9D3H0P1A/p1761136642568979?thread_ts=1761119656.960289&cid=C9D3H0P1A\n\nFurthermore, previously we'd create the tags automatically in the\n`prisma-engines` repo for all Prisma releases, including dev and\nintegration. However, we did not create tags for dev and integration\nreleases in the main repo, which sometimes was slightly annoying when\nbisecting or reproducing issues. Now every release will always be\ntagged, regardless of the release type.",
          "timestamp": "2025-11-04T19:19:30+01:00",
          "tree_id": "72e5c6dbee14509583476b3fd293b24efc8c7fa8",
