          "id": "54af19c0ac72e8389b2909b2c370036af497cb79",
          "message": "fix(ci): don't interpret explicit \"false\" as true in publish script (#28498)\n\nDespite `type: boolean` in the descriptions of some workflow inputs, all\nthese parameters are actually strings at run time. Thus, an explicit\n`\"false\"` value (e.g. from an unchecked checkbox in the GitHub UI) was\nbeing incorrectly interpreted as truthy in JavaScript.",
