          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d81b4b6396dc78619c84b526dbae6a8eba812456",
          "message": "fix: allow env generic with interfaces (#28694)\n\n## Fixes #28617\n\n### Problem\n\nThe `env` helper rejected interface-based environment variable types\nbecause the previous generic constraint\n`Env extends Record<string, string | undefined>` required an index\nsignature that interfaces don’t have.\nThis caused `TS2344` when following the documented example.\n\n### Fix\n\nThe type definition of `env` was updated and a new `EnvKey` helper type\nwas introduced to filter valid keys.\nThis allows both interfaces and type aliases to work as expected without\nchanging runtime behavior.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- Updated `env` signature using a simplified generic pattern  \n- Added `EnvKey` to restrict keys to `string | undefined` values  \n- Added a type-level test ensuring interface + type alias compatibility\n- Kept all runtime logic untouched  \n\n### Result\n\n- Interface support now matches documentation  \n- Type aliases continue to work  \n- Compile-time validation preserved  \n- Backwards-compatible with no runtime impact\n\nCo-authored-by: Florian Gößler <florian.goessler@hey.com>",
          "timestamp": "2025-12-03T09:22:25+01:00",
          "tree_id": "04f761cd8854ad70717f8895b54eaf5f45a32a81",
          "url": "https://github.com/prisma/prisma/commit/d81b4b6396dc78619c84b526dbae6a8eba812456"
