          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d00dc11af0859a7c9bc289f5e48df79a72ec046f",
          "message": "feat: add `traceContext` SQL commenter plugin (#28802)\n\nThis restores the functionality lost in Prisma 7 / QC.\n\nPreviously QE would always append the `traceparent` comments to the SQL\nqueries when tracing was enabled, adding unnecessary overhead and\nprepared statement hit misses (on MySQL; we solved the problem for\nPostgreSQL back then by using `tokio_postgres`'s `query_typed`).\n\nConversely, `QueryInterpreter` in QC architecture doesn't implement\n`traceparent` support at all, so users relying on that functionality\nhave reduced observability.\n\nThis PR makes use of the new SQL commenter plugin system to add an\nopt-in mechanism for appending `traceparent` comments to SQL queries\nonly for those users who want it.\n\nCloses:\nhttps://linear.app/prisma-company/issue/TML-899/build-trace-context-plugin\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added SQL Commenter Trace Context plugin to include W3C traceparent in\nsampled queries\n* Added an instrumentation-contract package exposing get/set/clear\nglobal tracing helpers\n* Prisma client can opt into query comments via a new comments\ninitialization option\n\n* **Refactor**\n* Centralized tracing helper management to use the new contract-based\nglobal accessors\n\n* **Tests**\n* Added unit and end-to-end tests validating trace-context behavior and\nglobal helper integration\n\n* **Chores**\n  * CI updated to run additional test suites\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can customize this high-level summary in your review\nsettings.</sub>\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
          "timestamp": "2025-12-03T12:35:49+01:00",
          "tree_id": "e54d671a690dfc82640cdf6b8b51fdf30715bc8b",
