          "distinct": true,
          "id": "bebccbddfd4db51785a21606e0524d123b2d65bd",
          "message": "feat(cli): customize `prisma init` based on the JS runtime (Bun vs other) (#28903)\n\nThis PR:\n- closes\n[TML-1672](https://linear.app/prisma-company/issue/TML-1672/prisma-init-customize-bun-experience-add-bun-support-to-e2e-tests)\n- updates the `prisma.config.ts` file generated by `prisma init`\n- adds Bun support to `e2e` tests\n- adds a new `prisma-init-bun` e2e test\n\n**Before this PR**\n\n`prisma init` would unconditionally generate the following\n`prisma.config.ts` file:\n\n```typescript\n// This file was generated by Prisma and assumes you have installed the following:\n// npm install --save-dev prisma dotenv\nimport \"dotenv/config\";\nimport { defineConfig, env } from \"prisma/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  schema: \"prisma/schema.prisma\",\n  migrations: {\n    path: \"prisma/migrations\",\n  },\n  datasource: {\n    url: env(\"DATABASE_URL\"),\n  },\n});\n```\n\n**After this PR**\n\n`prisma init` generates different `prisma.config.ts` files, depending on\nthe JS runtime used.\n\n- Bun, via `bun run --bun prisma [command]`\n\n  ```ts\n// This file was generated by Prisma, and assumes you run Prisma\ncommands using \\`bun --bun run prisma [command]\\`.\n  import { defineConfig, env } from \"prisma/config\";\n\n  export default defineConfig({\n    schema: \"prisma/schema.prisma\",\n    migrations: {\n      path: \"prisma/migrations\",\n    },\n    datasource: {\n      url: env(\"DATABASE_URL\"),\n    },\n  });\n  ```\n\n  Note that Bun automatically loads `.env` variables for us.\n\n- Node.js / other, via e.g. `npx prisma [command]`, `pnpm prisma\n[command]`, `bunx run prisma [command]`, `bun run prisma [command]` etc\n\n  ```ts\n// This file was generated by Prisma and assumes you have installed the\nfollowing:\n  // npm install --save-dev prisma dotenv\n  import \"dotenv/config\";\n  import { defineConfig } from \"prisma/config\";\n\n  export default defineConfig({\n    schema: \"prisma/schema.prisma\",\n    migrations: {\n      path: \"prisma/migrations\",\n    },\n    datasource: {\n      url: process.env[\"DATABASE_URL\"],\n    },\n  });\n  ```\n\n  Notice how `env()` is no longer used by default.\n\n---\n\nNote: the only guaranteed way I found of running Prisma via Bun is `bun\nrun --bun prisma [command]` (as per\nhttps://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/3417#issuecomment-1927842420).\n`bunx run prisma [command]` and `bun run prisma [command]` both use the\nNode.js runtime due to our [Node.js-specific\nshebang](https://github.com/prisma/prisma/blob/dbada5738682d577ea9b4f5c66ce435486a2f360/packages/cli/helpers/build.ts#L48)\n(see https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/3417).\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n## Release Notes\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added Bun runtime support to `prisma init` command, which now\ngenerates runtime-appropriate configuration for Bun environments.\n\n* **Tests**\n* Added end-to-end tests to verify correct configuration generation when\nusing Bun as the runtime.\n* Enhanced test infrastructure with Bun installation and configuration\nin Docker and test environments.\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can customize this high-level summary in your review\nsettings.</sub>\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jkomyno <12381818+jkomyno@users.noreply.github.com>",
