          "message": "fix(cli): remove Prisma Pulse from CLI help message (#29093)\n\n## Description\nRemoves the reference to Prisma Pulse from the CLI help message since\nPulse is currently paused/deprecated as of\nearly 2025.\n## Context\nPrisma Pulse was paused in early 2025 while being rebuilt based on user\nfeedback. The CLI help message was still\nadvertising it as an available product, which is misleading to users.\nThis PR updates the help message to only mention Prisma Accelerate,\nwhich is still actively available.\n## Changes\n- Updated `CLI.ts` to remove Pulse mention from help message\n- Kept the original `/cli/pdp` link\n### Before:\n  \nOptimize performance through connection pooling and caching with Prisma\nAccelerate\nand capture real-time events from your database with Prisma Pulse.\nLearn more at https://pris.ly/cli/pdp\n### After:\n                      \nOptimize performance through connection pooling and caching with Prisma\nAccelerate.\nLearn more at https://pris.ly/cli/pdp\n## References\n- Fixes: https://github.com/prisma/prisma/issues/29082\n- [GitHub Discussion about Pulse\ndeprecation](https://github.com/prisma/prisma/discussions/26508)\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Updated CLI help messaging for the Prisma Pulse feature with an added\nresource link for users to learn more.\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can customize this high-level summary in your review\nsettings.</sub>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
