          "id": "aef8cb57f395f1d3499d8c472f44306a63cd4aa7",
          "message": "fix(cli): remove the migrate-reset tool from the MCP server (#29691)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `prisma mcp` server exposed a `migrate-reset` tool that runs `prisma\nmigrate reset --force`. The MCP server is consumed exclusively by AI\nagents, and `migrate reset` drops the database — a destructive operation\nthat should not be offered to agents as a first-class tool at all, even\nbehind the AI safety checkpoint.\n\n## Solution\n\nRemove the `migrate-reset` tool from the MCP server, and note the\ndeliberate omission in `AGENTS.md`. An agent that genuinely needs a\nreset must run the CLI, where the AI safety checkpoint in\n`@prisma/migrate` (#29684) detects the agent and requires explicit user\nconsent via `PRISMA_USER_CONSENT_FOR_DANGEROUS_AI_ACTION`.\n\nEarlier commits on this branch pinned the safety checkpoint's behavior\n*through* the MCP tool; the later commits supersede them by removing the\ntool entirely (this PR is meant to be squash-merged).",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-08T15:09:18+02:00",
          "tree_id": "5cf5880fe9d7f8e2299e7a82541efaf364feda3e",
