          "message": "fix(migrate): guard db push data loss for AI agents (#29713)\n\n## Summary\n\n- run the AI safety confirmation checkpoint before `prisma db push\n--accept-data-loss` applies a forced schema push\n- add command-level regression coverage for both `--accept-data-loss`\nand `--force-reset`\n- document the expanded checkpoint scope in `AGENTS.md`\n\n## Why\n\n`db push --force-reset` already invoked the AI safety checkpoint, but\n`--accept-data-loss` was passed directly to the schema push engine. An\nAI agent could therefore opt into destructive schema changes without\nobtaining the explicit user consent required by the existing safety\nprotocol.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `TEST_NO_DOCKER=1 pnpm --filter @prisma/migrate test DbPush.test.ts\n--runInBand -t \"triggers the AI safety checkpoint\"`\n- existing non-agent `--accept-data-loss` test\n- `packages/migrate/src/__tests__/utils/ai-safety.test.ts`\n- Prettier and ESLint on changed files\n- `pnpm --filter @prisma/migrate build`\n\nThe full database-backed `DbPush` cases were not available locally\nbecause PostgreSQL and MongoDB were not running.",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-10T16:40:53+02:00",
