          "distinct": true,
          "id": "32978749ee248e25a31e035196c1bf376db31fa6",
          "message": "fix: close comment block in generated JS file preamble (#28960)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes #28949 \n\nThis PR fixes an issue where Biome linting would fail on generated\nPrisma Client files when using Prisma with tools like create-t3-app.\n\n\nThe first comment was missing the closing `*/`, which caused the\n`biome-ignore-all` directive to not work properly. This resulted in\nBiome reporting hundreds of linting errors on the generated Prisma\nClient files.\n\n\n### Testing\nThe TypeScript generator already has the correct syntax, and existing\ntests verify the presence of the biome-ignore directive (which will\ncontinue to pass).\n\nThis fix ensures the Biome ignore directive works correctly and prevents\nlinting errors on generated Prisma client files when used with\nBiome-based projects.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Resolved a syntax error in generated code preamble that could cause\ncompilation issues with generated files.\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can customize this high-level summary in your review\nsettings.</sub>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nCo-authored-by: Oleksii Orlenko <alex@aqrln.net>",
