          "distinct": true,
          "id": "800f1d1090a3bb110e2c76cc68c739cb545cc731",
          "message": "fix(adapter-pg): preserve constraint name for unique violations (23505) (#29587)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `23505` (unique violation) branch of `mapDriverError` in\n`@prisma/adapter-pg` extracted field names from `error.detail` via regex\nbut **ignored `error.constraint`**, while the `23503` (foreign key)\nbranch already prefers `error.constraint` as `{ index }`.\n\nThis asymmetry means unique violations lose the constraint/index name.\nFor partial unique indexes that share the same columns (e.g. a full\nunique on `(user_id, account_id)` and a partial unique on `(account_id)\nWHERE role = 'owner'`), the resulting errors become indistinguishable\nwithout reaching into non-public fields.\n\n## Fix\n\nAlign the `23505` handler with `23503`: prefer `error.constraint` as `{\nindex }`, falling back to the parsed `{ fields }` when no constraint\nname is present. Added a regression test.\n\nFixes #29495\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Oleksii Orlenko <alex@aqrln.net>\nCo-authored-by: Alexey Orlenko's AI Agent <robot@aqrln.net>",
