          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a50a33307c6dd0ffbe6d57473d2140209aa7cdbc",
          "message": "fix(build): use require.resolve to find Wasm files (#29445)\n\nWhen using pnpm, dependencies can get hoisted and won't always show up\nin local `node_modules`. The build scripts were using hardcoded paths to\nfind Wasm files, which broke in these setups. Using\n`require.resolve(...)` lets NodeJS find the files on its own, so the\nbuild works regardless of how the package manager structures the\ndependencies.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Updated Wasm file lookups in `packages/cli/helpers/build.ts` and\n`packages/internals/helpers/build.ts` to use `require.resolve` instead\nof hardcoded paths\n- Cleaned up old path variables that were no longer doing anything\nuseful\n- Noted the `require.resolve` pattern in `AGENTS.md` so future\ncontributors know why it's done this way\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexey Orlenko's AI Agent <robot@aqrln.net>",
