          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c5809e7f66258e1ef735e029ffd0b6d2ceb54208",
          "message": "ci(benchmark): stop alerting on Benchmark.js wall-clock results (#29804)\n\nThe `Store benchmark result` step in `benchmark.yml` compared each\ncommit against its immediate predecessor and both commented on the\ncommit and failed the workflow when the ratio exceeded 2x, CCing a list\nof individual handles.\n\n## Why this does not work\n\nGitHub-hosted runner throughput varies by more than 2x between jobs,\nwhich is wider than the spread this comparison would need to resolve.\nFrom the stored history on `gh-pages` (`dev/bench/data.js`), the last\nfew data points for `findUnique by id`:\n\n```\n2026-07-27 b64e33c9c 4455 ops/sec\n2026-07-27 6b6d9e90b 5259 ops/sec\n2026-07-28 3fa65ac13 9129 ops/sec\n2026-07-28 ac845368e 4485 ops/sec   <- flagged as a 2.04x regression\n```\n\n`ac845368` is the direct child of `3fa65ac1` and changed nothing but\n`.github/workflows/*`. Its parent happened to land on a fast runner, so\nthe next commit was charged with the difference:\nhttps://github.com/prisma/prisma/commit/ac845368eba4047a790440984dd5e1041093f28f#commitcomment-194035538\n\nThe failure mode runs both ways. A spurious speed-up at commit N\nmanufactures an alert at commit N+1, and a genuine regression smaller\nthan the machine-to-machine spread is never reported at all. No value of\n`alert-threshold` sits above the noise floor and below a regression\nworth catching.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `comment-on-alert: false` and `fail-on-alert: false`; drop the\nnow-unused `alert-threshold` and `alert-comment-cc-users`. `auto-push`\nstays, so the chart at https://prisma.github.io/prisma/dev/bench/ keeps\ngetting data points.\n- Regression detection is left to the CodSpeed step in the same job,\nwhich runs the same benchmarks under simulation and is not subject to\nrunner variance.\n- Update the job's fork guard comment, which referenced\n`alert-comment-cc-users`.\n- Record the reasoning in `AGENTS.md` so the silent alerter is not\nmistaken for a threshold that wants tuning.\n\nRemoving `alert-comment-cc-users` also retires a CC list that named two\npeople who no longer work at Prisma. If we want the ORM team notified of\nreal regressions, that belongs in the CodSpeed project settings rather\nthan here; its alert threshold is currently `>100%` and may be worth\ntightening separately.\n\n## Scope\n\nCI configuration and `AGENTS.md` only. No benchmark code, no product\ncode. Verified with `actionlint 1.7.1`.",
