          "distinct": true,
          "id": "103e67ce6092b70c5a06fdd40687d81603b9362a",
          "message": "ci: drop the workflows that now run from the default branch (#29824)\n\n## Summary\n\nCompanion to prisma/prisma#29821, which moves these three workflows to\nthe default branch. This removes the copies left behind here.\n\nGitHub reads cron schedules only from the default branch, so none of the\nthree ever fires on this branch — their schedules are inert. On the\ndefault branch, CodeQL scans this branch by checking it out explicitly\nand attributing its results back to this ref, while the stale-issue and\ndiscussion bots act on repository objects that belong to no branch at\nall.\n\nLeaving inert copies behind invites the wrong one to be edited, and\nleaves `codeql-analysis.yml` with two different definitions at one path\nacross the two branches — the more confusing because a dispatch against\nthis ref would run *this* copy.\n\n| Removed | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `.github/workflows/codeql-analysis.yml` | 47 |\n| `.github/workflows/label-stale-issues.yml` | 22 |\n| `.github/workflows/auto-close-github-discussions.yml` | 46 |\n| `.github/workflows/scripts/auto-close-github-discussions.js` | 266 |\n\n## Deliberately left alone\n\nThe root `package.json` keeps `@octokit/rest` and `@octokit/graphql`.\nThe removed script was their only consumer on this branch, so both are\nnow unused — but dropping them requires regenerating `pnpm-lock.yaml`,\nwhich is a different kind of change and does not belong in a\nworkflow-removal diff. Worth a follow-up.\n\n## Ordering\n\nBest merged after prisma/prisma#29821, so the repository is never\nwithout these workflows on either branch. Nothing actually breaks if it\nlands first, since the schedules here do not run in any case.\n\n## Testing performed\n\n- Swept the branch for references to all three workflows and the script:\nthe only one is the discussion workflow's own `run:` line, which goes\nwith it.\n- Confirmed `@octokit/rest` and `@octokit/graphql` have no other\nconsumer on this branch, which is what the note above rests on.\n- A deletion cannot be exercised beforehand. The check that matters is\nthat prisma/prisma#29821 has landed, so the automation exists on the\ndefault branch.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] All commits are signed off per the DCO.\n- [x] The change is scoped to one logical concern.\n\nSigned-off-by: Alexey Orlenko's AI Agent <robot@aqrln.net>",
